    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="7" relname="concession">P24, I agree-it is very frustrating to lose work.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="8" relname="span">Most computer users have been told to save their work often.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="evidence">Saving your work often is emphasized in most computer courses.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="9" relname="span">At this point, most of us are acutely aware of how important it is to save our work often.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="elaboration">This cliché is based (at least in part) on the poor error recovery of many user interfaces, especially some of the earlier applications and operating systems.</segment>
        <group id="6" type="span"/>
        <group id="7" type="span" parent="6" relname="span"/>
        <group id="8" type="span" parent="7" relname="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="8" relname="evidence"/>
    </body>
